age-relative application ID: \n```\n```\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7270) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11600K @ 3.90GHz (12 threads)\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720945064/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721162815","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-2721162815","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":2721162815,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iMaY_","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T12:55:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T12:55:37Z","body":"Can you reproduce this after switching `rendering_driver.windows` to `d3d12` in the Project Settings then restarting the editor?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2721162815/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722992398","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-2722992398","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":2722992398,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iTZEO","user":{"login":"Ticxo","id":41558177,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNTU4MTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41558177?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo","html_url":"https://github.com/Ticxo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ticxo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-14T00:23:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-14T00:23:16Z","body":"Changing that to `d3d12` seems to have stopped it from happening.\n\nI did some more testing with before switching. Not sure if these would be useful but here are my experience:\n- I swapped the driver to `d3d12`, noticed that it was throwing lots of error on a particular texture (not square, not powers of 2 width and height,) and decided to switch back to `vulkan` and managed to encounter no crash for an hour\n- After the initial crash, the crashes happen a lot more frequently. Ranges between 1 to 10 minutes.\n- Somehow for one session the engine lasted an hour before crashing again. I didn't do anything out of the ordinary in that session\n- Sometimes I can \"predict\" the crash happening when shaders and materials have their color picker stuck at being white. Not sure if it is a coincident or actually related\n- Deleting the `imported` and `shader_cache` in `.godot` doesn't seem to reduce the crash\n- When the engine crashes while the game is running on a popped out window, the window itself closes but the game would still run until I interact with it\n\nI didn't rigorously write notes on what I did before it crashes. Overall the engine crashes very randomly under normal usecase. I kept a backup of the project using vulkan and I will post updates if I found more information.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722992398/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3023757117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-3023757117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":3023757117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60Ot89","user":{"login":"NuclearPhoenixx","id":17517687,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTE3Njg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17517687?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx","html_url":"https://github.com/NuclearPhoenixx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T12:15:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T16:31:57Z","body":"Having the exact same issue that you describe it with `dxgi.dll, Version: 10.0.26100.4484` and exception code `0xc000001d` with a custom build from the up-to-date 4.4 branch on Windows 11 (using a single custom module and `precision=double`, otherwise default build).\n\nWhen I worked more with Godot last year, I already had that same issue and never found a reason or solution for it, it was insanely annoying to deal with because it happened fairly regular, similar to how you mentioned. Now I noticed that problem again, and found this issue fortunately, I'm happy someone had a deeper look into it. The crashes don't seem to occur that often anymore, but it's still highly disruptive, especially if you don't constantly save everything. I would say it happens once per hour or so on my machine average.\n\n(The only thing that doesn't work for me is changing to `d3d12` (game crashes instantly), but that might be because of a custom module that I'm using, I don't really care about that, would rather use Vulkan anyways.)\n\nDefinitely sounds like a rendering issue, maybe related to graphics drivers on Windows? Happy to hear your thoughts.\n\nI already tried the following to no avail:\n- Clean re-install graphics drivers with Nvidia DDU\n- Memory check with MemTest86+\n- sfc /scannow\n- DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth\n- CHKDSK /F\n\nUpdate: Just noticed that Godot doesn't even seem to realize it crashed. Normally, if the editor crashes it asks you if you wanted to load the project normally or restore it or something. It doesn't do that after this crash.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3023757117/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024969376","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-3024969376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":3024969376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60TV6g","user":{"login":"AeioMuch","id":75151379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MTUxMzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75151379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch","html_url":"https://github.com/AeioMuch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AeioMuch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T17:42:11Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T18:00:49Z","body":"@NuclearPhoenixx Something that you can try, as a workaround, is to go in your NVIDIA control panel -> Manage 3D settings -> Program settings -> Select or Add your Godot executable -> Vulkan/OpenGL present method -> Choose native mode\n\nThat's what I suggested months ago on discord to the person behind this related/duplicate issue : https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104140 (even tho they mention forced DX12, it's also DXGI, same settings)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024969376/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3025342188","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-3025342188","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":3025342188,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60Uw7s","user":{"login":"SlimyFrog123","id":89934852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTM0ODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89934852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123","html_url":"https://github.com/SlimyFrog123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlimyFrog123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-01T20:02:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-01T20:02:57Z","body":"> @NuclearPhoenixx Something that you can try, as a workaround, is to go in your NVIDIA control panel -> Manage 3D settings -> Program settings -> Select or Add your Godot executable -> Vulkan/OpenGL present method -> Choose native mode\n> \n> That's what I suggested months ago on discord to the person behind this related/duplicate issue : https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104140 (even tho they mention forced DX12, it's also DXGI, same settings)\n\nThis seems to work for me. I tried it a couple days ago and it seemed to help — just waiting to make sure it wasn't a fluke.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3025342188/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033159848","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-3033159848","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":3033159848,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60ylio","user":{"login":"NuclearPhoenixx","id":17517687,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTE3Njg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17517687?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx","html_url":"https://github.com/NuclearPhoenixx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuclearPhoenixx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T18:19:49Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T18:19:49Z","body":"> [@NuclearPhoenixx](https://github.com/NuclearPhoenixx) Something that you can try, as a workaround, is to go in your NVIDIA control panel -> Manage 3D settings -> Program settings -> Select or Add your Godot executable -> Vulkan/OpenGL present method -> Choose native mode\n> \n> That's what I suggested months ago on discord to the person behind this related/duplicate issue : [#104140](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104140) (even tho they mention forced DX12, it's also DXGI, same settings)\n\nI can also confirm this works. Awesome, thanks!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3033159848/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3046324593","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-3046324593","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":3046324593,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61kzlx","user":{"login":"VicPrzz00","id":148383236,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNgmBA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148383236?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00","html_url":"https://github.com/VicPrzz00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T19:40:55Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T19:40:55Z","body":"> Having the exact same issue that you describe it with `dxgi.dll, Version: 10.0.26100.4484` and exception code `0xc000001d` with a custom build from the up-to-date 4.4 branch on Windows 11 (using a single custom module and `precision=double`, otherwise default build).\n> \n> When I worked more with Godot last year, I already had that same issue and never found a reason or solution for it, it was insanely annoying to deal with because it happened fairly regular, similar to how you mentioned. Now I noticed that problem again, and found this issue fortunately, I'm happy someone had a deeper look into it. The crashes don't seem to occur that often anymore, but it's still highly disruptive, especially if you don't constantly save everything. I would say it happens once per hour or so on my machine average.\n> \n> (The only thing that doesn't work for me is changing to `d3d12` (game crashes instantly), but that might be because of a custom module that I'm using, I don't really care about that, would rather use Vulkan anyways.)\n> \n> Definitely sounds like a rendering issue, maybe related to graphics drivers on Windows? Happy to hear your thoughts.\n> \n> I already tried the following to no avail:\n> \n>     * Clean re-install graphics drivers with Nvidia DDU\n> \n>     * Memory check with MemTest86+\n> \n>     * sfc /scannow\n> \n>     * DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth\n> \n>     * CHKDSK /F\n> \n> \n> Update: Just noticed that Godot doesn't even seem to realize it crashed. Normally, if the editor crashes it asks you if you wanted to load the project normally or restore it or something. It doesn't do that after this crash.\n\nExactly the last sentence, which makes it even harder to understand what is causing it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3046324593/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3046325394","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99315#issuecomment-3046325394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99315","id":3046325394,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61kzyS","user":{"login":"VicPrzz00","id":148383236,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNgmBA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148383236?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00","html_url":"https://github.com/VicPrzz00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VicPrzz00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T19:41:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T19:41:19Z","body":"> > [@NuclearPhoenixx](https://github.com/NuclearPhoenixx) Something that you can try, as a workaround, is to go in your NVIDIA control panel -> Manage 3D settings -> Program settings -> Select or Add your Godot executable -> Vulkan/OpenGL present method -> Choose native mode\n> > That's what I suggested months ago on discord to the person behind this related/duplicat